{"number": 244, "text": "                                                                                                Appendix    4\n\n                  | Negative short forms (see Unit 41):\n                      isn’t     (= is not)     don't     (= do not)    can’t        (= cannot)\n                                               doesn’t   (=doesnot)    couldn’t             not)\n                      wasn’t    (=wasnot)      didn’t    (=didnot)     won't        (= will not)\n                      weren’t   (= were not)                           wouldn’t     (= would not)\n                              = (= has not)                            shouldn’t    (= should not)\n                      haven’t   (= have not)                            mustn’t     (= must not)\n                      hadn’t       had not)\n\n                         ©  We  went  to her house, but she wasn’t home.\n                         ©   “Where's David?”  “I don’t know. | haven’t seen him.”\n                         ©   You work all the time. You shouldn’t work so hard.\n                         ©   |won’t  be here tomorrow. (=| will not)\n\n            [4.5  |  ’s (apostrophe + s)\n                     ’s can mean different things:\n                     (1)   =is or has (see section 4.2 of this appendix)\n                         ©)  It’s raining. (= It is raining)\n                         ©)  It’s been raining all day! (= It has been raining)\n                     (2) let’s = let us (see Unit 34 and Unit 51)\n                         ©   It’s a beautiful day. Let’s go outside. (= Let us go outside.)\n\n                     (3)  Kate’s camera = her camera\n                          my brother’s car = his car\n                          the manager’s office = his/her office, etc.\n                          (see Unit 62)\n                     Compare:\n                         ©   Kate’s camera was very expensive. (Kate’s camera = her camera)\n                         ©   Kate’s a very good photographer. (Kate’s = Kate is)\n                         ©   Kate’s got a new camera. (Kate’s got = Kate has got)\n\n\n                                                                                                              233", "char_count": 2182, "mean_conf": 86.53, "word_count": 228, "words": [{"text": "Appendix", "x0": 1972, "y0": 95, "x1": 2197, "y1": 146, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "4", "x0": 2209, "y0": 97, "x1": 2236, "y1": 132, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "4.4", "x0": 248, "y0": 225, "x1": 346, "y1": 309, "conf": 27, "bold": false}, {"text": "|", "x0": 367, "y0": 225, "x1": 388, "y1": 309, "conf": 78, "bold": false}, {"text": "Negative", "x0": 417, "y0": 246, "x1": 584, "y1": 291, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "short", "x0": 599, "y0": 243, "x1": 698, "y1": 280, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "forms", "x0": 712, "y0": 242, "x1": 821, "y1": 279, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "(see", "x0": 835, "y0": 241, "x1": 910, "y1": 287, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "Unit", "x0": 925, "y0": 243, "x1": 1009, "y1": 278, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "41):", "x0": 1023, "y0": 240, "x1": 1090, "y1": 285, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "isn’t", "x0": 446, "y0": 320, "x1": 530, "y1": 373, "conf": 78, "bold": false}, {"text": "(=", "x0": 650, "y0": 324, "x1": 690, "y1": 370, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "is", "x0": 707, "y0": 326, "x1": 731, "y1": 360, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "not)", "x0": 746, "y0": 323, "x1": 826, "y1": 368, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "don't", "x0": 955, "y0": 318, "x1": 1065, "y1": 372, "conf": 70, "bold": false}, {"text": "(=", "x0": 1160, "y0": 321, "x1": 1200, "y1": 366, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "do", "x0": 1216, "y0": 322, "x1": 1267, "y1": 358, "conf": 95, "bold": false}, {"text": "not)", "x0": 1282, "y0": 320, "x1": 1363, "y1": 365, "conf": 91, "bold": false}, {"text": "can’t", "x0": 1463, "y0": 319, "x1": 1566, "y1": 356, "conf": 64, 